  "chapter": {
    "number": 11,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(12) For the end, A Psalm of David, upon the eighth."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Save me, O Lord; for the godly man has failed; for",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 23
          },
          {
            "text": "truth is diminished from among the children of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Every one has spoken vanity to his neighbor: their lips are deceitful, they have spoken with a double heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let the Lord destroy all the deceitful lips, and the tongue that speaks great words:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who have said, We will magnify our tongue; our lips are our own: who is Lord of us?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because of the misery of the poor, and because of the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, says the Lord, I will set them in safety; I will speak to them thereof openly.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The oracles of the Lord are pure oracles; as silver tried in the fire, proved in",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 24
          },
          {
            "text": "a furnace of earth, purified seven times.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You, O Lord, shall keep us, and shall preserve us, from this generation, and for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The ungodly walk around: according to your greatness you have greatly exalted the sons of men.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 23,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. truths are become rare",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 11,
          "verse": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 24,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. the earth.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 11,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
